cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SMART-Wound, please cite the article describing it (listed under 'preferred-citation')."
title: "SMART-Wound: a texture-based ImageJ/Fiji plug-in for wound / scratch-assay segmentation and quantification"
abstract: >-
  SMART-Wound is a free, open-source ImageJ/Fiji plug-in that segments the
  cell-free area in in-vitro wound-healing (scratch) assays using a local-texture
  map with divisive illumination normalisation, so that the migrating-cell front
  is delineated robustly across illumination gradients and irregular wound shapes,
  excluding inter-cell gaps of the confluent monolayer.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/FRJT-BIO/SMART-WOUND"
url: "https://github.com/FRJT-BIO/SMART-WOUND"
keywords:
  - ImageJ
  - Fiji
  - wound healing assay
  - scratch assay
  - cell migration
  - texture segmentation
  - image processing
